<% content_for :title, "Deleting your account · VIVUM Plants" %>
<% content_for :help_page, "1" %>

<header class="grid gap-1">
  <p class="vv-kicker">Help</p>
  <h1>Deleting your VIVUM Plants account</h1>
</header>

<p>
  You can delete your account yourself, on the web or in the app. It's the same
  page in both.
</p>

<h2>How to delete your account</h2>

<ol>
  <li>Sign in and open <strong>Account</strong> (Settings → Account).</li>
  <li>Choose <strong>Delete my account</strong>.</li>

  <li>
    Enter your password, and your two-step code if you use one, then confirm.
  </li>
</ol>

<p>
  If you're the only owner of a seller business, make another member an owner
  first, or ask us to close the business.
</p>

<h2>What happens</h2>

<ul>
  <li>
    Your account is switched off and you're signed out everywhere at once.
  </li>

  <li>
    After 30 days we delete your profile, plants, photos, settings,
    notifications and sign-in details. Sign in before then to keep your account.
  </li>

  <li>
    We keep a record of the terms you agreed to and our security log for up to
    two years, so we can show what was agreed and investigate misuse. Neither
    holds your email address. Backups expire within 90 days.
  </li>

  <li>
    Sales records a seller business keeps about orders you placed belong to that
    business; ask the seller about those.
  </li>
</ul>

<p>
  Want a copy of your data first? Choose <strong>Export my data</strong> on the
  same page. To ask about anything else we hold, use Settings → Privacy, or see
  the <%= link_to "privacy notice", legal_privacy_path %>.
</p>
